# 🧠 Research Vault - Decentralized Paper Repository
**Research Vault** is a decentralized application (DApp) that allows researchers to upload, store, and prove authorship of research papers on the Ethereum blockchain, while leveraging IPFS for decentralized file storage and zkSNARKs for privacy.

## 🚀 Features

### ✅ Level 1: Core Functionality
- Upload research papers (PDFs).
- Store paper metadata (title, author, timestamp, IPFS hash) on Ethereum.
- Public feed of uploaded papers.
- IPFS integration for decentralized file storage.

### 🎓 Level 2: Soulbound NFTs
- Automatically mint a **soulbound NFT** on each successful upload.
- NFTs contain paper metadata and prove authorship.
- Non-transferable (soulbound) nature prevents misuse.

### 🔐 Level 3: ZK Proof Integration
- Upload with a zero-knowledge proof to verify ownership without revealing paper contents.
- ZK-SNARK circuit built using Circom & SnarkJS.

---

## 🧩 Tech Stack

| Layer        | Tech                      |
|-------------|---------------------------|
| Blockchain   | Ethereum (Hardhat)        |
| Storage      | IPFS (via `Pinata`) |
| ZK Proofs    | Circom, SnarkJS           |
| Frontend     | React.js                  |
| Styling      | CSS       |
| Contracts    | Solidity, OpenZeppelin    |

## 📁 Project Structure
research_vault/
├── contracts/             # Smart contracts (Solidity)
├── scripts/               # Deployment and test scripts
├── zk/                    # Circom circuits and SnarkJS outputs
├── frontend/              # React frontend app
│   ├── public/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── App.js
│   │   ├── App.css
│   │   └── contract/
├── .env                   # Environment variables (gitignored)
├── hardhat.config.js      # Hardhat setup


## ⚙️ How to Run Locally

```bash
git clone https://github.com/PrinceBisht22/princebisht_spider-task1-.git
cd princebisht_spider-task1-/domain_specific/blockchain/research_vault

# Install dependencies
cd frontend
npm install

# Start the React frontend
npm start

# In a new terminal, go back to root and run:
npx hardhat node
npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.cjs --network localhost
